WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.320
Which video game adaptations were&nbsp;
originally slated for the silver screen?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.160
What award-winning family drama&nbsp;
was almost a movie about octuplets?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.200
Check out which TV shows were&nbsp;
originally planned to be movies.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.560
The gun-slinging bounty hunter from a galaxy&nbsp;
far, far away had a tumultuous journey before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.320
finally landing on the Disney streaming service.&nbsp;
Shortly after Disney acquired Lucasfilm and, by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.440
extension, the "Star Wars" franchise, the company&nbsp;
announced spin-off films telling stories adjacent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.880
to the original "Star Wars" saga. "Boba Fett" was&nbsp;
initially supposed to be one of those projects:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.840
originally, Josh Trank, the director of&nbsp;
"Chronicle" and the catastrophic box-office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.840
bomb that was 2015's "Fantastic Four," pitched&nbsp;
his version of a Boba Fett narrative to Lucasfilm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:49.120
The studio was enthusiastic about his ideas and&nbsp;
announced his admission to the "Star Wars" family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.560
with Trank set to direct the&nbsp;
Boba Fett standalone production.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.280
After the failure and drama that spun out&nbsp;
of "Fantastic Four," Trank quit the project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.560
understanding that he'd probably be&nbsp;
fired if he didn't drop out himself.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.280
Eventually, the project landed in the&nbsp;
hands of "Logan" director James Mangold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.560
but a certain famous fictional smuggler seemingly&nbsp;
ruined plans for Boba's big-screen future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.800
The prequel film "Solo: A Star Wars Story," which&nbsp;
chronicled Han Solo's younger days picking fights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.520
with gangsters and the Empire, was considered&nbsp;
a financial disappointment upon its release.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.640
Disney's focus shifted toward&nbsp;
their new streaming service,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.680
where "The Mandalorian" became a flagship series&nbsp;
for the service's debut. Thanks to that show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.480
success, plans for Boba Fett's own series&nbsp;
quickly followed, and the rest is history.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:42.080
George R. R. Martin's "A Song of Ice and Fire"&nbsp;
novels are now as well-known as Tolkien's Middle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.840
Earth fantasy thanks to the additional popularity&nbsp;
that the HBO series "Game of Thrones" brought to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.560
the books. For years, Martin had been courted&nbsp;
by scriptwriters who eagerly wanted to share&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.360
their version of Martin's fantasy world in&nbsp;
live-action cinema. Like a King's Landing not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.560
fit for the Dragon Queen's world, he scorched&nbsp;
these ideas to ash and cinder. According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.840
Entertainment Weekly in 2011, Martin claimed&nbsp;
that his book series was simply unfilmable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.560
despite visions to the contrary attempting&nbsp;
to sell him on the idea. The author stated,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:18.800
"Even Tolkien took three feature films, and three&nbsp;
Tolkien [novels] are as long as one of my books."

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.120
Martin also noted that, after giving a&nbsp;
feature-film idea some thought, he felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.720
that his works were simply too mature. After all,&nbsp;
sex and violence saturate the entire narrative.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.120
"Be quick about it."

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.800
Eventually, David Benioff and D.B. Weiss&nbsp;
approached Martin and proposed adapting his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.720
books into a series. Since the show would land on&nbsp;
HBO, the mature content was no longer a problem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.880
Furthermore, Benioff and Weiss could take&nbsp;
all the time they needed to build out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.520
story over several seasons, depending on&nbsp;
the show's popularity. After reaching an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.080
accord with Martin on the direction of the&nbsp;
series, film ideas were finally put to rest.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.480
The White Wolf, better known as Geralt of Rivia,&nbsp;
has long been a mainstay of the fantasy genre.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.400
Andrzej Sapkowski created the fabled&nbsp;
Witcher and authored a collection of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.040
stories surrounding his exploits before&nbsp;
writing a sprawling saga. The Witcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.400
known for his combat prowess, keen senses, and&nbsp;
hunting acuity, is capable of slaying the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.840
dangerous of monsters in the wilds. Geralt is&nbsp;
also often embroiled in the warring politics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.160
evil machinations, and drama of the most&nbsp;
prominent characters to populate the land.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.760
Netflix was always a prime destination for the&nbsp;
Witcher to receive a proper live-action outing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.400
Although the character had appeared in a few&nbsp;
well-received video games made by Polish game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:42.480
developer CD Projekt RED, fans were chomping at&nbsp;
the bit to see Geralt realized in cinematic glory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.160
"The Witcher" was originally going&nbsp;
to receive a standalone Netflix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.320
film, but creatives behind the scenes&nbsp;
convinced the producers that there was far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.120
too much material to cover in just two hours.&nbsp;
Convinced that the property deserved more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.960
they got the green light to move&nbsp;
forward with a Netflix original series.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:04.080
"Mr. Robot" was a massive hit for the USA&nbsp;
Network. Centered around a mentally unwell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.440
cybersecurity expert named Elliot, the series&nbsp;
deals with hacktivism and political issues of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.760
all kinds. It received high praise from&nbsp;
both critics and audiences along the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.600
winning three Emmys, two Golden&nbsp;
Globes, and a Peabody Award.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.880
"I respect that about you."

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:24.320
However, many likely don't realize that&nbsp;
"Mr. Robot" was originally intended to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.160
be an independently produced feature&nbsp;
film. In an interview with Forbes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:32.720
series creator Sam Esmail discussed&nbsp;
his creative journey. Esmail stated,

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.480
"When I saw it as a movie, I knew&nbsp;
where I was going. I knew the ending."

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.360
The problem was that he simply had more material&nbsp;
than he knew what to do with. Esmail continued,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.040
"When I got to page 90 and I&nbsp;
was still halfway through Act 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.640
that's when I decided, 'OK.&nbsp;
This can be a television show.'"

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.920
The showrunner still tackled the&nbsp;
series like a movie production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.440
treating each episode as if it&nbsp;
were a short film. Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.000
Esmail still achieved what he set out to do&nbsp;
with the narrative he'd originally planned.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.960
Sure, the fiery vigilante of Hell's Kitchen&nbsp;
already received a big-screen adaptation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.240
in 2003 with Ben Affleck taking on the&nbsp;
role of the blind lawyer Matt Murdock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:15.280
However, the Netflix "Daredevil" series was&nbsp;
also originally envisioned and pitched as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:20.240
film by series creator Drew Goddard. Goddard&nbsp;
explained why the film approach ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:25.680
didn't pan out in an interview with IGN: Marvel&nbsp;
nixed the idea, believing that Goddard's approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.080
was far too dark and violent. Marvel&nbsp;
simply wouldn't do an R-rated film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.200
Furthermore, Daredevil is typically seen as a&nbsp;
local hero, interested primarily in cleaning the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.920
streets of his own neighborhood. That wouldn't&nbsp;
gel with the large-scale epics of the MCU.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.880
Instead, "Daredevil" landed on Netflix, with&nbsp;
Goddard free to produce his far more mature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.800
take on the character. Goddard, who'd&nbsp;
previously stated that anything short&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.720
of his adult vision would be inadequate,&nbsp;
was certainly pleased with this outcome.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.880
Believe it or not, "The Sopranos"&nbsp;
was originally destined for theaters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.120
Imagine seeing James Gandolfini's&nbsp;
Tony Soprano on the silver screen:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.960
it would have been a sight to behold.&nbsp;
However, this hypothetical film wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.920
have been the cultural landmark that "The&nbsp;
Sopranos" series was across its six seasons.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.080
According to series co-creator David&nbsp;
Chase, the show was conceived as a film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.080
and pitched as such from the get-go.&nbsp;
However, Chase's manager at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:22.480
Lloyd Braun, suggested that his idea&nbsp;
could actually be a television series.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.480
Chase gave it some thought and began to wrap&nbsp;
his mind around the mobster's life as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:31.600
ongoing series. The scope of his pitch&nbsp;
changed, but only enough to cover Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:36.160
ending with Tony confronting his mother over&nbsp;
trying to kill him. Chase understood this moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.880
as the end of their tormented relationship, and&nbsp;
the second season had to work with fresh ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.440
beyond the scope of Chase's original plan. In&nbsp;
the end, of course, Chase produced one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.880
best TV dramas in history, which won 21 Emmys and&nbsp;
five Golden Globes during its time on the air.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.320
"I'm honored just to be considered."

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:59.360
The winding family drama "This Is Us" likes&nbsp;
to toy with viewers' emotions. The story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:04.000
follows the Pearson clan and their three&nbsp;
children, who are depicted at various ages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:09.760
but primarily as adults. They experience many of&nbsp;
life's greatest joys and heartaches. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:14.720
the Pearsons and many other supporting characters&nbsp;
reflect many facets of American society.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:19.200
While the series has proved to be one of the&nbsp;
most successful dramas in modern television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.800
it wasn't always meant to depict&nbsp;
the same family that we know today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:28.000
In an interview with Emmy Magazine, series&nbsp;
creator Dan Fogelman revealed some juicy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.520
details regarding the origins of the show. Instead&nbsp;
of Randall, Kate, and Kevin as the "Big Three,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:39.520
Fogelman originally penned an 80-page film&nbsp;
featuring a Pearson family with octuplets.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:44.560
Ultimately, Fogelman decided that he didn't want&nbsp;
to follow a traditional narrative trajectory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:49.360
with a beginning, middle, and end. He wanted&nbsp;
to explore a lasting story that continuously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:53.840
unfolded in the past, present, and future&nbsp;
of a single family. The character-driven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:58.480
nature of the show has proved successful,&nbsp;
engaging audiences and critics alike. Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:02.720
just be thankful that we didn't have to&nbsp;
follow the chaotic lives of octuplets.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:05.360
"Dumb luck."

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:13.040
In 2020, "The Queen's Gambit" took the streaming&nbsp;
world by storm with a thrilling period piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:19.200
based on the 1983 novel by Walter Tevis. The&nbsp;
Netflix miniseries centers around Beth Harmon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.400
portrayed by Anya Taylor-Joy. As an orphaned&nbsp;
youth, she becomes obsessed with and shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.640
a talent for chess, eventually developing&nbsp;
a drug addiction to help her focus on her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:33.680
game and cope with personal loss. The series&nbsp;
chronicles her rise to fame in the chess world.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:39.040
"The Queen's Gambit" novel had long been examined&nbsp;
for a possible feature film adaptation. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.160
the late actor Heath Ledger, himself something of&nbsp;
a chess connoisseur, was planning on making his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:49.280
directorial debut with an adaptation of the&nbsp;
novel before he tragically passed away. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:54.080
project was halted upon Ledger's death, and was&nbsp;
eventually pitched to Netflix as a miniseries.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:59.920
Fans of the original Archie Comics likely never&nbsp;
suspected that it would eventually be adapted for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:05.760
the small screen in live-action. The television&nbsp;
series on the CW Network, titled "Riverdale,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:11.600
features the exploits of the famous Archie Comics&nbsp;
teenagers, including Archie Andrews, Betty Cooper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:17.040
Jughead Jones, and Veronica Lodge. Positioned&nbsp;
as a teen drama, "Riverdale" goes big on its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:23.280
mystery themes and has enjoyed a lasting legacy&nbsp;
on the CW network with its deliciously dark tones.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:27.440
Of course, Archie almost found himself&nbsp;
on the big screen. Warner Bros. sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:32.480
an adaptation of the character on film. The&nbsp;
creatives behind the TV series originally had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:37.760
their idea dismissed and were asked to work on&nbsp;
Archie's first-ever live-action appearance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:42.800
a time-traveling story featuring Louis C.K.&nbsp;
of all people as the iconic high schooler.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.760
The studio imagined a Riverdale filled with&nbsp;
portals that would open up to other dimensions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:52.320
That was just a little too wacky, a bit too&nbsp;
much like a live-action "Rick and Morty."

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.280
Thankfully, "Riverdale" show creator Robert&nbsp;
Aguirre-Sacasa didn't like that idea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.120
He walked away from the whole ordeal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:03.840
only to be contacted later by the studio to&nbsp;
commit his original vision to television.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:08.640
Like the bounty-hunting Boba Fett,&nbsp;
Jedi Master extraordinaire Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:12.160
Kenobi was once set to return to&nbsp;
the big screen in his own film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:18.560
After "Solo: A Star Wars Story" didn't exactly&nbsp;
gain the financial returns Lucasfilm and Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:23.440
were looking for, their approach shifted focus.&nbsp;
The streaming service Disney Plus changed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.800
game for Lucasfilm, giving Ewan McGregor a chance&nbsp;
to reprise his role on the streaming platform.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.040
"Hello, there."

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:36.240
In fact, both Ewan McGregor and Hayden&nbsp;
Christensen are set to reprise their prequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:41.840
film roles in the "Obi-Wan Kenobi" series. The&nbsp;
show offers fans the chance to finally see what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:47.200
Obi-Wan has been up to for all those lonesome&nbsp;
years in the desert wilderness of Tatooine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.800
While his top goal is to protect&nbsp;
Luke Skywalker, it seems that much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:54.560
more went on behind the scenes than&nbsp;
Luke could've ever possibly imagined.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:11:00.320
As a live-action production, the popular video&nbsp;
game property "Halo" has been through development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:06.240
hell and back. Aside from smaller productions like&nbsp;
"Forward Unto Dawn" and "Nightfall," a true-blue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:12.080
Halo film with Master Chief positioned as the&nbsp;
lead has been in the works as far back as 2005.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:17.760
Alex Garland, known for "Ex Machina" and&nbsp;
"Annihilation," was hired by Microsoft to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:23.040
write an adaptation of the series for the silver&nbsp;
screen. Guillermo del Toro was attached to direct,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.960
but ran for the exit when he decided to&nbsp;
head up "Hellboy II: The Golden Army."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:32.800
The project eventually bounced over to "District&nbsp;
9" creator Neill Blomkamp, but a tug-of-war over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:38.000
creative control between Fox, Universal, and&nbsp;
Microsoft resulted in the project being shelved.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:42.240
"Halo" once again entered the live-action&nbsp;
spotlight with the announcement of a TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:48.080
series in 2013 with Steven Spielberg attached&nbsp;
as a producer. News emerged that the series was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:52.080
being developed for Showtime. After going&nbsp;
through several producers and directors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:57.040
the show was shifted to Paramount Plus,&nbsp;
where it made its debut in March 2022.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.880
Now, "Halo" has received the renewed&nbsp;
attention it deserves in the live-action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.040
space — although that might be up&nbsp;
for debate among longtime fans.

